      "writtenOn": "2026-09-01T13:48:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m trying to figure out if it matters or not, or even what we\u0027d prefer the behavior to be. But I\u0027m wondering for this and the drawable case when we do nesting if we want to count the drawPicture or drawDrawable as an op itself. So this would turn into `fCount +\u003d 1 + op.picture-\u003eapproximateOpCount(true)`.\n\nPart of my reasoning is that if we have a picture/drawable with zero internal ops, if we have nested is false then it will return 1 and if we nested as true it will return 0. In my head I feel like they should match, but maybe not???",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 396,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 396,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "d9029fb60001401d7deea9d99ba03cae2215b83f",
